{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/ModulesAndProtocolBindings","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Documentation index"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein","type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitle":"Documentation index"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/skein\/modulesandprotocolbindings"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"article","title":"Modules and protocol bindings","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Skein"}]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/BindingsAndLifetimes","doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/Qualifiers"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules keep registrations close to the feature that owns them. Application builders accept individual modules, arrays, optionals, conditions, and loops directly.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Skein","","protocol HTTPClient {","    func get(path: String) throws -> String","}","","final class URLSessionClient: HTTPClient {","    func get(path: String) throws -> String { \"response\" }","}","","final class ArticleRepository {","    private let client: any HTTPClient","","    init(client: any HTTPClient) {","        self.client = client","    }","}","","let networking = module {","    single((any HTTPClient).self, provider: { _ in URLSessionClient() })","}","","let articles = module {","    factory(ArticleRepository.self, using: ArticleRepository.init)","}","","try startSkein {","    networking","    articles","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The binding key is the declared type, not the concrete type returned by the provider. Register a protocol existential such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(any HTTPClient).self"},{"type":"text","text":" when consumers depend on the protocol. Resolve the same declared type inside providers and at call sites."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let client = try get((any HTTPClient).self)","let repository: ArticleRepository = try get()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All modules are collected during application creation. Registering the same type and qualifier twice, whether in one module or separate modules, fails creation with a source-aware "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkeinConfigurationError"},{"type":"text","text":" whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"underlying"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkeinError.duplicateBinding"},{"type":"text","text":". Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/Qualifiers","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" when multiple implementations of one type are intentional."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Test or environment overlays","anchor":"Test-or-environment-overlays"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"overriding(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" creates a reusable module where registrations in the overlay replace exact binding keys from the base module. Duplicates within either input module still fail when an application is created."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let production = module {","    single((any HTTPClient).self, provider: { _ in URLSessionClient() })","}","final class PreviewHTTPClient: HTTPClient {","    func get(path: String) throws -> String { \"preview\" }","}","let preview = module {","    single((any HTTPClient).self, provider: { _ in PreviewHTTPClient() })","}","","let previewApplication = try SkeinApplication {","    production.overriding(preview)","}"]}]}],"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://Skein/documentation/Skein/Qualifiers":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/skein\/qualifiers","title":"Qualifiers","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/Qualifiers","abstract":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Documentation index"}],"overridingTitle":"Documentation index","identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein"}]},"doc://Skein/documentation/Skein/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting started","identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/GettingStarted","abstract":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein","overridingTitle":"Documentation index","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Documentation index"}],"type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/skein\/gettingstarted","kind":"article"},"doc://Skein/documentation/Skein/BindingsAndLifetimes":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/skein\/bindingsandlifetimes","title":"Bindings and lifetimes","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein\/BindingsAndLifetimes","abstract":[{"overridingTitle":"Documentation index","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Documentation index"}],"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein","isActive":true}]},"doc://Skein/documentation/Skein":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Skein\/documentation\/Skein","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Skein is a small, type-safe dependency-injection container for Swift."}],"role":"collection","title":"Skein","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/skein"}}}